decisions:
  - id: conductor-macos-first
    decision: Build macOS-native with Swift/SwiftUI, defer Windows to future port
    rationale: Native gives best UX, access to Apple Vision (Neural Engine) and WhisperKit (CoreML). 7 abstraction protocols ensure Windows port doesn't require rewrite.
  - id: conductor-zero-cost
    decision: All ML inference runs locally — zero paid APIs, zero subscriptions
    rationale: Aligns with Paradigm philosophy of empowering developers without extracting. WhisperKit and MediaPipe are both free and run on-device.
  - id: conductor-ships-with-paradigm
    decision: Conductor ships as part of @a-company/paradigm, not a separate package
    rationale: Tight integration with paradigm-mcp for context enrichment, Sentinel for status, workspace for multi-project awareness. One install, one command.
  - id: conductor-sprint-symbol-gates
    decision: Register Paradigm symbols via MCP at each sprint gate
    rationale: Conductor eats its own dogfood — every sprint completion requires recording new components, flows, gates, signals, and aspects in the .purpose file via MCP tools.
learnings:
  - Voice-to-buffer staging with gesture editing is a fundamentally different interaction model than typing — it separates composition from dispatch
  - Apple Vision framework on Neural Engine gives essentially free hand pose detection at 15fps, making gesture input viable without GPU overhead
  - MediaPipe FaceMesh is the only viable cross-platform gaze solution — works identically on macOS and Windows
  - Sprint 1 being camera-free (keyboard + window detection + manual send) means Conductor is immediately useful even before the multimodal features land
  - Context enrichment via paradigm-mcp subprocess per project means each Claude Code window gets project-specific context automatically — this is the killer integration point
tags:
  - arc:conductor
